description:
Write function helpers and a class with events.

```csharp
public static class Fn
{
    public static Func<T, T> Pipeline<T>(params Func<T, T>[] steps)        // applies the steps left to right
    public static Func<T, TResult> Memoize<T, TResult>(Func<T, TResult> f) where T : notnull
    public static Action Once(Action action)                              // runs action the first time only
}

public record PriceChange(string Symbol, decimal Old, decimal New)
{
    public decimal Percent { get; }      // (New - Old) / Old * 100, rounded to 2 decimals
}

public class StockTicker
{
    public event EventHandler<PriceChange>? PriceChanged;
    public event EventHandler<PriceChange>? BigMove;
    public void Update(string symbol, decimal price)
}
```

- `Pipeline()` with no steps returns its input unchanged.
- `Memoize` calls `f` once per distinct argument and returns the stored result after that.
- `StockTicker.Update` remembers the last price per symbol. The first price of a symbol raises nothing. A different price raises `PriceChanged`, and then also `BigMove` when the change is 5 % or more either way. The same price again raises nothing. The sender of each event is the ticker.

